<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walloons</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Walloons are the French-speaking people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, named after the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallonia">Wallonia</a>. From the twelfth century groups of Walloons, together with Flemings and Germans, settled as privileged 'guests' in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, especially in and around towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szekesfehervar">Székesfehérvár</a> and Eger, where they had their own quarters and liberties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walloons.jpg" alt="Walloons" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tom Lemmens · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Wallonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
